After a terribly depressing run of losing three characters on the Astral 
Plane within a week to stupid deaths I recovered rather well: this was 
my third ascension in thirteen games (the others were a Barbarian and a 
Tourist). It was also my third quickest ascension, at 22331 turns.

A fairly normal start: attempted the protection racket, made it to 
Minetown at XL:2. Found some speed boots quite early on. Sokoban had a 
bag of holding. In the mines, picked up a mattock to clear some space to 
kick-test a gray stone. The mattock was cursed. Whoops. After several 
attempts to dip it in fountains, tried prayed. Hermes was not impressed. 
Whoops, there goes my protection. I eventually got rid of the mattock 
and mollified Hermes.

There was a black dragon on the Quest Home level: not something to take 
on without reflection, so I continued on in the Dungeon. At Medusa, a 
master lich disintegrated my boots. Got to the castle without much 
trouble, played with the drawbridge, and grabbed the wand. A gray dragon 
dropped scales, which I turned into GDSM. Wished for ?oCharging, speed 
boots, and a magic marker. Found another wand of wishing on Medusa's 
level and a shield of reflection in Perseus's statue.

Headed for the Quest, where a blue dragon blew up the wands of wishing, 
which I forgot to put in my bag. Whoops. Fortunately, I ran into one of 
my bones piles (drowned by a python on the Locate level) which had 
several useful items: SDSM, CoMR, Excalibur (via a HoOA), Vorpy two 
magic lamps. I switched to SDSM/CoMR/Excalibur to take on the Cyclops. 
Took the Staff up to Hippocrates, who told me I'd forgotten the Bell. 
Whoops. Back down, got the Bell and back up.

Went through Gehennom, paid off Asmo and Baal. At Juiblex's, wished for 
a ring of levitation. Except I already had one. Whoops. Killed Juiblex 
and Orcus, found the Vibrating Square, went to Rodney and stoned him -- 
over the water. Zapped a wand of teleportation at the water, picked up 
the Book, headed for the Square. And I'd forgotten the Candelabrum. 
Whoops. Went off to kill Vlad, knocked over Rodney who paid a visit on 
the way, got the Candelabrum and went for the Amulet.

Picked up gauntlets of power in the Sanctum. Rodney double-troubled  I 
stoned him both. The RNG was strangely benevolent: I was mysteriously 
forced only once on the entire run. Did some alchemy, wrote some 
scrolls, headed for the Planes. Re-learnt the extra healing spell. Made 
it to Astral fairly quickly. Death was behind door number one, so I 
avoided him and went for door two with Famine. Knocked him down a couple 
of times, offed some priests and Angels, made it to the altar: chaotic. 
Headed for door number three, killed Pestilence, killed more priests and 
Angels. A master lich summoned a few nasties; I broke a wand of 
teleportation to get some breathing space. I decided to use a ring of 
conflict to get the monsters off my back. Made it into the temple, 
removed the ring: neutral. Offered the Amulet. You all know what happens 
next.

